<!-- 01 — THE SITUATION -->
<section class="container measure section-block section-block--tight">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">01 — The situation</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">Translation is the smallest part</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">What counts as premium in the home market is average in a technologically more advanced market — and simply too expensive in another. The same product then needs a different justification for its price, not just a different sentence.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">On top of that come labelling requirements that differ from country to country, and trademark systems in which a name or a pack is judged differently than at home.</p>
  <p class="pull-quote reveal reveal-delay-2">Consistent in its craft, local in its address — otherwise it is either arbitrary or expensive.</p>
</section>

<!-- 02 — WHAT IS CREATED -->
<section class="container measure section-block">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">02 — What is created</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">One core, many versions</h2>
  <ul class="check-list">
    {%- for item in [
      "Multilingual packaging with the labelling required in each target market",
      "Videos on a shared image base with language-specific lettering — produced, not merely conceived, in up to 20 languages",
      "Sales material that justifies the price in each market instead of repeating the home market",
      "Checks on likelihood of confusion and trademark law in the target countries, while the design is being developed",
      "A documented separation between what stays the same everywhere and what may adapt"
    ] %}
    <li class="check-item reveal reveal-delay-{{ loop.index0 % 3 }}">
      <span class="check-icon"></span>
      <span>{{ item }}</span>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

